Title: HV 24-Shot Benchmark
Credit: version 1.0.0 (frozen fixture — changes require a version bump and baseline re-record)

INT. LIGHTHOUSE - NIGHT

A storm lashes the glass.

KEEPER
The light stays on.

EXT. CLIFF PATH - NIGHT

Rain hammers the stone steps.

INT. RADIO ROOM - NIGHT

Static crackles from an old set.

KEEPER
Anyone out there?

EXT. SEA - NIGHT

A small boat climbs a black wave.

INT. BOAT CABIN - NIGHT

A lantern swings. Water at the boots.

SAILOR
Almost home.

EXT. HARBOR - DAWN

The storm breaks. Gulls wheel.

INT. LIGHTHOUSE - DAWN

The keeper douses the lamp.

EXT. DOCK - DAY

The sailor ties off the line.

SAILOR
Saw your light.

INT. KITCHEN - DAY

Two mugs of tea steam on a table.

KEEPER
It stays on.

EXT. CLIFF PATH - DAY

They walk up together.

INT. LAMP ROOM - DAY

Sunlight through the great lens.

EXT. LIGHTHOUSE - SUNSET

The beam sweeps the darkening sea.

INT. RADIO ROOM - SUNSET

The keeper logs the day.

EXT. SEA - NIGHT

Calm water. Starlight.

INT. LIGHTHOUSE - NIGHT

The lamp turns, steady.

EXT. CLIFF PATH - NIGHT

The sailor climbs with a parcel.

INT. KITCHEN - NIGHT

Bread broken between friends.

SAILOR
For the light.

EXT. HARBOR - NIGHT

Boats sleep at their moorings.

INT. LAMP ROOM - NIGHT

Hands polish the brass.

EXT. SEA - DAWN

First light on the water.

INT. RADIO ROOM - DAWN

A new voice on the static.

VOICE
Thank you, keeper.

EXT. LIGHTHOUSE - DAY

The tower stands in full sun.

INT. LIGHTHOUSE - DAY

The keeper smiles, winds the clock.

EXT. CLIFF PATH - SUNSET

Two figures against the sky.
